<h2>New sign-in to the admin panel</h2>

<p>Your admin account (<%= @admin.email %>) was just used to sign in from a browser or device it has not been used on before.</p>

<p><strong>When:</strong> <%= @signed_in_at.in_time_zone('Asia/Dhaka').strftime('%-d %B %Y, %-I:%M %p') %> (Bangladesh time)</p>

<p><strong>Device:</strong> <%= @browser %></p>

<p><strong>IP address:</strong> <%= @ip %></p>

<p style="color:#666;font-size:13px;"><%= @user_agent %></p>

<p><strong>Was this you?</strong> Then there is nothing to do. You will not get this email again for this browser.</p>

<p><strong>Not you?</strong> Someone may know your admin password. Change it straight away: sign in to the admin panel, open Admin Users, edit your account and set a new password. Then check Admin Users for any account you do not recognise.</p>
